---
import Sub from '../layouts/Sub.astro';
import { cityPageSchema, SERVICE_PAGES } from '../data/site.js';

const description =
  'Concrete sealing in Ivins and Kayenta, Utah — architectural concrete, driveways, patios and pool surrounds against Snow Canyon. Clear penetrating finishes that protect without changing the look.';

const schema = cityPageSchema({
  path: '/concrete-sealing-ivins-ut',
  city: 'Ivins',
  description,
});
---

<Sub
  title="Concrete Sealing in Ivins & Kayenta, UT | Armour Crete"
  description={description}
  crumb="Ivins, UT"
  schema={schema}
>
  <Fragment slot="h1">Concrete sealing<br />in Ivins &amp; Kayenta.</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    Up against Snow Canyon, the concrete is part of the architecture — and the
    right protection is the kind you cannot see. Clear penetrating sealers that
    leave the surface looking exactly as the architect intended, on driveways,
    patios, pool surrounds and the stone beside them.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="aside">
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>100%</dt><dd>Transparent — the clear sealer changes nothing about the look</dd></div>
      <div><dt>0</dt><dd>Films to yellow, peel or strip</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Free</dt><dd>On-site assessment, anywhere in Ivins</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <p class="eyebrow">Services in Ivins, UT</p>
        <h2 class="display sec-h">Everything we do,<br />done quietly.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="chips rv">
        {SERVICE_PAGES.map((s) => <li><a href={s.href}>{s.label}</a></li>)}
      </ul>
      <div class="prose rv" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <p>
          In Kayenta and the newer custom builds around Ivins, the brief is
          usually the same: protect the surface without announcing it. The clear
          penetrating sealer dries one hundred percent transparent — no film, no
          sheen, no sign it is there. Where a surface is meant to read richer,
          <a class="tlink" href="/wet-look-concrete-sealing">enhancement from
          within</a> deepens the material's own colour without laying plastic
          over it. And travertine or stone around a pool gets its
          <a class="tlink" href="/pool-deck-sealing">own product</a>, because
          stone stains in ways that do not come back out.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-dark">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="rv">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-lt">Red rock, red dust</p>
        <h2 class="display sec-h">The desert is the view.<br />It is also the problem.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose rv">
        <p>
          The same exposure that makes Ivins worth building in works on the
          concrete every day: hard UV, hundred-degree seasonal swings, winter
          nights below freezing, and the iron-red dust that finds its way into
          every open pore. A sealed surface gives the dust nowhere to lodge and
          the water nowhere to sit — the slab rinses clean instead of staining,
          and the freeze–thaw cycle is starved of the moisture it needs.
        </p>
        <p>
          On architectural concrete the prep matters as much as the product:
          cracks corrected, <a class="tlink"
          href="/expansion-joint-replacement">joints re-filled</a> cleanly, and
          the sealer applied in the early morning before the slab takes on heat,
          because a flash-dried finish streaks — and on a surface this visible,
          streaks are the whole story.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <p class="eyebrow">Ivins questions</p>
        <h2 class="display sec-h">Asked in<br />Ivins.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq rv">
        <details class="qa">
          <summary>Will sealing change how our concrete looks?</summary>
          <div class="qa-b"><p>
            Only if you choose that. The clear penetrating sealer is fully
            transparent; enhancement and wet-look finishes deliberately deepen
            colour. We show you both on your own surface before anything is
            committed to.
          </p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="qa">
          <summary>Can you work around landscaping and finished surfaces?</summary>
          <div class="qa-b"><p>
            Yes — the products are water-based and solvent-free, and the
            application is controlled. Protecting what is next to the concrete is
            part of the job, not an extra.
          </p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="qa">
          <summary>How long is the surface out of use?</summary>
          <div class="qa-b"><p>
            Twenty-four hours before you walk or drive on it. One day, told to
            you straight, so nobody finds out on the way to dinner.
          </p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Sub>
